<article class="env-definition" id="0536">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0536">Definition <span data-tag="0536">15.22.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a domain. Let $M$ be an $R$-module. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say an element $x \in M$ is <em>torsion</em> if there exists a nonzero $f \in R$ such that $fx = 0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $M$ is <em>torsion free</em> if the only torsion element of $M$ is $0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $M$ is a <em>torsion module</em> if every element of $M$ is torsion. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>